The primary divisors are~$\mathcal{P}=\{nv_1,nv_2,\dots,nv_{n-1},q\}$ and for
each~$j=0,1,\dots,n-1$, the
secondary divisors for~$D_j$ are
\[
  \mathcal{S}_{[D_j]}=
  \textstyle
  \left\{ \left((a_1+j)\bmod n,a_2,\dots,a_{n-2},\sum_{i=1}^{n-2}ia_i\bmod n,0\right):0\leq
  a_i<n\text{ for~$i=1,\dots,n-2$} \right\}.
\]
For example, in the case~$n=4$ and~$j=2$, we have~$16$ secondary divisors
for~$[D_2]\in\Jac(C_4)$:
\begin{align*}
  \mathcal{S}_{[D_2]}= \{ &
    (2, 0, 0, 0), (2, 1, 2, 0), (2, 2, 0, 0), (2, 3, 2, 0), (3, 0, 1, 0), (3, 1, 3, 0),
    (3, 2, 1, 0), (3, 3, 3, 0),
    \\[8pt]
